# Gobel coding standards

## Architecture

- **Gameplay rules live in effects + resolver**, not scattered `if card_id ==` / `if stone_id ==` in UI or `resolve_round`.
- **Definitions are immutable** (`objects/definitions/*`). Runtime changes use **instances** (`ObjectInstance`, `level`, hand/board snapshots).
- **Resolve at use time**: `content.get_*` for static defs; `content.resolve_stone(instance)` (and similar) when level/upgrades/tags matter.
- **Card targeting**: eligibility from **target-side tags** (`resolve_target_tags`); cards declare `required_tags_all` / `excluded_tags`, not hardcoded checks.
- **Validation is authoritative in resolver**; UI only mirrors `validate_card_targets` for buttons/hover — do not duplicate rules in `main.lua`.

```lua
-- ❌ BAD — UI-only legality
if card_id == "card_heal_1" and cell.solidity < max then ...

-- ✅ GOOD
local v = resolver.validate_card_targets(card_def, targets, state, actor)
if not v.ok then return end
```

## Code style (Lua)

- **Minimal diff** — no drive-by refactors or unrelated files.
- **Docstrings** (`--- @param`, `--- @return`) on new/changed functions; avoid inline comments for behavior.
- **Fully typed** new APIs: `str | nil`, not `Optional`; use Enums/tables with schema validation in `objects/schema.lua` for defs.
- **Small focused functions**; avoid deep nesting and copy-paste — extract shared logic once.
- **No gratuitous defensive branches** or `pcall` unless explicitly required.

## Data & state

- Prefer **domain shapes** (instances, board cells with `kind` + `level` + `solidity`) over anonymous nested dicts in business logic.
- **Snapshot on commit**: board/hand state at play time must not change when inventory upgrades later.
- **Parameters** (`objects/parameters/*`) for balance numbers; **definitions** for identity, effects, `max_level`, upgrade tables.

## Effects & scoring

- Effects use **`macro` + `sub`** (`territory`, `points`, `mult`); do not add one-off scoring branches in `resolve_round`.
- New card/stone behavior = new **effect_name** + `objects/effects.lua` factory + registry wiring + spec.

## Tests

- Add **unit tests** for validators, `apply_effect_deltas`, resolve helpers.
- Add **integration tests** for one end-to-end flow per feature; keep UI specs behavior-focused (state flags), not pixel tests.
- Run affected `spec/unit/*` and `spec/integration/*` before finishing.

## AI / search (when touching `ai/`)

- Do not call `resolve_round` from MCTS/search/planner paths.
- Keep latency budgets and prescore caps unless the user explicitly requests tuning.

## Commits & PRs

- One concern per PR; match existing naming and file layout.
- Do not commit secrets; do not amend/push unless the user asks.
